description:
FILED s513i (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-10, s514 resume) from the Text-CSV-2.04 board leg once Text::CSV loads (Encode shim, #2946).

HANG, pre-existing in PCL (reachable only now: before the shim every Text-CSV t/ file died at `use Text::CSV`): Text::CSV_PP's pure-Perl parser (`__parse` / `__get`, the LOOP / RESTART / EOLX labelled region with backward `goto RESTART` and `goto EOLX`, lib/Text/CSV_PP.pm ~2288-2830) never returns on some inputs.  perl returns at once.

    # scratch/s513i/c67.pl, run from an empty directory with PERL5LIB=cpan-tests/modules/Text-CSV-2.04/lib
    use strict; use warnings;
    use Text::CSV qw(csv);
    my $tfn = "_c67.csv";
    open my $fh, ">", $tfn or die; print $fh "a,b\n1,2\n\n3,4\n"; close $fh;
    print "before\n";
    my $r = csv(auto_diag => 0, in => $tfn, skip_empty_rows => 1);
    print "after ", scalar(@$r), "\n";      # perl: after 3    PCL: never prints (timeout)
    unlink $tfn;
    (skip_empty_rows => 0 returns 4 rows, = perl.)

VICTIMS: t/67_emptrow.t (stops at row 24 "A Skip"; perl 56 rows), t/41_null.t (hangs after row 31 in a getline over NUL-bearing fields; perl 128 rows) -- both TIMEOUT (rc=124) on the board.  A minimal backward-goto-into-a-loop-body program (scratch/s513i/g1.pl) is identical to perl, so the trigger is narrower: the skip-empty-row branch (`$c = $self->__get($ctx, $src); ... goto RESTART;` at line ~2620) re-entering RESTART with the EOL character.  Next step: instrument __get / the RESTART entry under PCL to see which variable stops advancing (`$ctx->{used}` / pos($ctx->{tmp}) after a `goto` back into the `while (... =~ /\G.../gs)` body is the first suspect -- a goto that re-enters the inner while may reset the match position).


ALSO t/71_pp.t (s514, after 6d36c1c9 let it past util.pl): stops after row 5 and runs to the board timeout (perl 104 rows) -- same family assumed, unverified.


=== DONE (s515a) ===
CAUSE: not goto.  A //g match whose TARGET is an ELEMENT ($ctx->{tmp} =~ /\G.../g) was passed to the matcher as its VALUE, so the pos state was keyed by the string object, while pos($ctx->{tmp}) read (and pos(...) = N wrote) the element's CELL: every read answered undef.  __get does `$ctx->{used} = pos($ctx->{tmp})`, so used never advanced and the skip-empty-row RESTART spun.  FIX: the target of a //g match that is an element is generated as its cell (ExprToCL lvalue_context 'matchcell' -> the -argbox heads; new runtime p-gethash-deref-argbox / p-aref-deref-argbox): the live slot when it exists, a lazy alias when not (no vivify, probed).  Also closes #1567 ($_[0] =~ /\G../gc).  csv67 oracle = perl.  Text-CSV alone: 41_null 128/0 (perl 128), 71_pp 104/0 (perl 104), 67_emptrow 50/6 (perl 56): the 6 (H Default/Skip/EOF/error/Callback/Callback 0) are bom => 1 header keys read as 'SCALAR(0x..)' -- PRE-EXISTING on the base, #3202.  Guard Pl/t/elem-pos-01.t (11, one TIMED row; 8 fail on the base).  Commit 36a6fb04 (s515a).
